@database "speech_gen"
@author "Enrico Ehrich"
@$VER: speech_gen.guide 1.0 (24.11.2026)
@smartwrap

@node main "Speech Generation"
@{h1}Speech Generation

The @{tt}speech_gen@{utt} plugin gives agents sandboxed access to text-to-speech
models configured under @{tt}llm_system.tts_models@{utt} and
@{tt}llm_system.tts_profiles@{utt} (such as Gemini TTS, ElevenLabs, and OpenAI /
OpenRouter Speech). Each call writes a 16-bit PCM WAV file inside the
instance's write sandbox and can optionally attach it as an audio preview for
audio-capable models.

Two tools, no hooks and no panel. Multiple instances can run side by side with
different sandboxes, profile allowlists, and character caps.

@{code}
For agents and developers
  @{"  synthesize  " link synthesize}
  @{"  list_profiles  " link list_profiles}
  @{"  What the model sees  " link model}
  @{"  Setting it up  " link setup}
@{body}
@endnode

@node synthesize "synthesize"
@{h1}synthesize

Calls @{tt}create_tts_from_profile@{utt} for the selected TTS profile and writes
the returned PCM audio atomically to @{tt}output_path@{utt} (must end in
@{tt}.wav@{utt}).

@{table}
Parameter | Meaning
text | required; text to speak (or speaker-labelled transcript when using @{tt}speakers@{utt}), at most @{tt}max_text_chars@{utt} characters
output_path | required; target @{tt}.wav@{utt} file path inside @{tt}output_directories@{utt}
profile | TTS profile from @{tt}llm_system.tts_profiles@{utt} (optional when @{tt}default_profile@{utt} is set)
voice | optional voice name or provider voice ID (overrides the model default; not with @{tt}speakers@{utt})
speakers | optional list of 1-2 @{tt}{name, voice}@{utt} objects for multi-speaker synthesis (where supported by the provider)
system_instruction | optional style or delivery direction (single-speaker only; providers with @{tt}supports_style_prompt=False@{utt} warn and ignore it)
seed | optional integer seed (single-speaker only; provider-dependent)
reference_audio | optional audio file path inside @{tt}input_directories@{utt} for voice cloning (only offered and accepted when @{tt}allow_voice_cloning: true@{utt})
reference_text | optional transcript of @{tt}reference_audio@{utt} (only with @{tt}reference_audio@{utt}; used by stateless speech APIs, ignored by providers that clone via upload)
attach_preview | @{tt}false@{utt} (default): set @{tt}true@{utt} to attach the WAV to the tool result when under the 25 MB audio attachment limit
@{body}

Returns @{tt}status: "success"@{utt} with @{tt}path@{utt},
@{tt}duration_seconds@{utt}, @{tt}sample_rate@{utt}, @{tt}channels@{utt},
@{tt}bytes@{utt}, @{tt}mime_type@{utt} (@{tt}audio/wav@{utt}), @{tt}profile@{utt},
@{tt}model@{utt}, optional @{tt}voice@{utt}, optional @{tt}warnings@{utt}, and
@{tt}not_attached@{utt} if @{tt}attach_preview@{utt} exceeded the request limit.
@endnode

@node list_profiles "list_profiles"
@{h1}list_profiles

Lists the TTS profiles allowed on this instance with their @{tt}description@{utt},
@{tt}model_ref@{utt}, @{tt}provider@{utt}, @{tt}model@{utt}, @{tt}default_voice@{utt},
and @{tt}is_default@{utt}, plus the instance's @{tt}allow_voice_cloning@{utt} and
@{tt}max_text_chars@{utt} settings.
@endnode

@node model "What the model sees"
@{h1}What the model sees

@{h2}Tool descriptions and errors

The schema lists allowed profiles as an enum when at least one profile is
configured, makes @{tt}profile@{utt} optional when @{tt}default_profile@{utt} is
set, and exposes @{tt}reference_audio@{utt} / @{tt}reference_text@{utt} only when
@{tt}allow_voice_cloning: true@{utt}. Validation errors (sandbox denial,
non-@{tt}.wav@{utt} path, text over @{tt}max_text_chars@{utt}, unsupported
multi-speaker or voice cloning, missing voice) return
@{tt}{"status": "error", "error": "..."}@{utt} before any API call.

@{h2}Token and cache effect

Append-only: each call returns one tool result. @{tt}attach_preview@{utt}
defaults to @{tt}false@{utt} because most chat models lack @{tt}audio_input@{utt}
and raw WAV attachments cost roughly 32 tokens per second on audio-capable
models. When enabled, the attachment is frozen by content hash so overwriting
the path later does not invalidate earlier turns in the prompt cache.

@{h2}Known gaps

@{bullet}@{tt}create_tts_from_profile@{utt} does not yet forward
@{tt}network.ssl_verify@{utt} to TTS provider clients.
@{bullet}@{tt}file_checkpoints@{utt} counts @{tt}speech_gen/synthesize@{utt} as
an untracked write rather than snapshotting previous bytes at @{tt}output_path@{utt}.
@{bullet}Output is always 16-bit PCM WAV; use @{" Audio operations " link audio_ops/main}
if you need MP3/FLAC conversion or post-processing.
@endnode

@node setup "Setting it up"
@{h1}Setting it up

Configure TTS models and profiles under @{tt}llm_system.tts_models@{utt} and
@{tt}llm_system.tts_profiles@{utt} in @{tt}config/llm.yaml@{utt}, then configure
an instance in @{tt}config/plugins.yaml@{utt}:

@{code yaml}
plugins:
  servers:
    speech_gen:
      type: speech_gen
      enabled: true
      output_directories:
        - "data/speech_gen"
      input_directories:
        - "data/speech_gen"
      default_profile: "gemini-tts"
      allow_voice_cloning: false
      max_text_chars: 5000
@{body}

@{table}
Key | Default | Meaning
output_directories | data/speech_gen | write sandbox (PathSandbox); empty refuses all writes
input_directories | same as output_directories | read-only sandbox for @{tt}reference_audio@{utt}
profiles | all configured | allowlist of @{tt}llm_system.tts_profiles@{utt}
default_profile | none | profile used when @{tt}synthesize@{utt} omits @{tt}profile@{utt}
allow_voice_cloning | false | opt-in gate for @{tt}reference_audio@{utt}
max_text_chars | 5000 | maximum characters per @{tt}synthesize@{utt} call
max_reference_size_mb | 15.0 | maximum size per @{tt}reference_audio@{utt} file in MiB
@{body}
@endnode
